Description: Simulates power for non-inferiority tests in repeated cross-sectional
    stepped-wedge cluster randomized trials with binary or continuous outcomes.
    The package supports exchangeable, nested exchangeable and AR(1)
    cluster-by-period correlation structures, a reference 'lme4' engine and
    batched PyTorch GPU and CPU acceleration with fused CUDA kernels (including
    zero-setup execution on Google Colab via 'reticulate' or a Python CLI),
    fixed categorical period adjustment, user-specified secular period effects,
    unequal numbers of clusters across sequences, unequal cluster-period sample
    sizes, parameter grids, reproducible optional parallelization, conservative
    handling of failed model fits, Monte Carlo standard errors, conversion of
    clinically specified margins to the model scale, a search for the smallest
    cluster-period size or number of clusters meeting a power target, optional
    Word export, and an optional Shiny interface.
